# Copy to .env.local and fill in values (never commit .env.local)

# Server-side sync script (npm run sync:lending-cc) — optional for other routes / offline CSV snapshots.
LENDING_CC_API_BASE_URL=https://lending-cc-staging.platform.mypaytm.com
LENDING_CC_API_TOKEN=

# Funnel Summary (/funnel-summary) loads only from ClickHouse in the browser via Lending CC POST /api/query.
# next.config.ts mirrors LENDING_CC_* into NEXT_PUBLIC_* at build/dev start, so filling only the LENDING_CC_*
# pair below is enough after you restart `next dev` or run `next build` (values are inlined into the client bundle).
NEXT_PUBLIC_LENDING_CC_API_BASE_URL=https://lending-cc-staging.platform.mypaytm.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_LENDING_CC_API_TOKEN=

# Security: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are embedded in the client bundle — anyone can read the token from built JS.
# Use a read-scoped token and rotate if leaked.

# CORS: direct browser POST to Lending CC is often blocked. In next dev / Vercel (non–static export), Next.js
# rewrites /lending-cc/api/query → your LENDING_CC host (see next.config). Static export (e.g. GitHub Pages)
# cannot proxy — the API must send CORS headers or you need an external BFF.
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_LENDING_CC_DIRECT=1 to force calling the Lending CC URL from the browser (only if CORS allows it).

# If the UI shows “HTTP 500” / non-JSON from Lending CC, the failure is server-side (often ClickHouse rejecting
# a query). Check Lending CC logs; validate columns in src/lib/lending-cc-sql.ts against your OLAP schema.

# ─── Vercel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. vercel.com → Add Project → Import this Git repo.
# 2. Settings → General → Root Directory = "dashboard" (required: Next.js lives in dashboard/).
# 3. Settings → Environment Variables: add the same NEXT_PUBLIC_LENDING_CC_* (and optional LENDING_CC_* for
#    server rewrites). Production/Preview/Development as needed. VERCEL=1 is set by Vercel at build/runtime.
# 4. Deploy. Optional: repo root .github/workflows/vercel-production.yml + VERCEL_TOKEN, VERCEL_ORG_ID,
#    VERCEL_PROJECT_ID if you deploy via GitHub Actions instead of Vercel’s Git integration (avoid both).
